SELECT src
FROM (
  SELECT type, name, line AS ord,
         CASE WHEN line = 1 THEN 'CREATE OR REPLACE ' END
         || RTRIM(text, CHR(10) || CHR(13)) AS src
  FROM   all_source
  WHERE  owner = 'CES'
  AND    type IN ('PROCEDURE','FUNCTION')
  UNION ALL
  SELECT type, name, MAX(line) + 1, '-----------'
  FROM   all_source
  WHERE  owner = 'CES'
  AND    type IN ('PROCEDURE','FUNCTION')
  GROUP  BY type, name
)
ORDER BY type, name, ord;

It returns all standalone functions first, then all procedures, each ending with -----------.

If you want them in separate files, change the two type IN ('PROCEDURE','FUNCTION') lines to type = 'PROCEDURE' or type = 'FUNCTION' and run it twice.

If it returns no rows, run this to see which schema owns them, then put that name in place of 'CES':

sql
SELECT owner, object_type, object_name
FROM   all_objects
WHERE  object_type IN ('PROCEDURE','FUNCTION')
AND    owner NOT IN ('SYS','SYSTEM','XDB','MDSYS','CTXSYS','ORDSYS','OUTLN','DBSNMP','WMSYS')
ORDER  BY owner, object_type, object_name;
